    "PR description: \"SelectionResult::Clear() removes the selected inputs but keeps their bump fee discount. GetTotalBumpFees() then subtracts that discount from zero, so any positive discount gives the empty selection a negative fee total. The wallet currently avoids this because it only clears selections inside the knapsack solver, before applying the discount.\"",
    "Commit 4ce6b53149: \"The discount accounts for shared ancestors of the selected inputs. Once those inputs are gone, subtracting their discount gives the empty selection a negative bump fee total.\""
